  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n8 5 0\n8 5 3\n0 3 2\nOutput:\n8 5 0 0 8 8\n8 5 3 3 5 5\n0 3 2 2 3 0\n0 3 2 2 3 0\n5 5 3 3 5 8\n8 8 0 0 5 8\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n3 8 2\n3 2 2\n8 5 2\nOutput:\n3 8 2 8 3 3\n3 2 2 5 2 8\n8 5 2 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 5 8\n8 2 5 2 2 3\n3 3 8 2 8 3\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n0 3 0\n6 6 6\n0 3 0\nOutput:\n0 3 0 0 6 0\n6 6 6 3 6 3\n0 3 0 0 6 0\n0 6 0 0 3 0\n3 6 3 6 6 6\n0 6 0 0 3 0\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n2 5 0\n2 5 1\n3 1 1\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(grid: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform an N\u00d7N grid into a 2N\u00d72N grid composed of four quadrants:\n    - top\u2011left: original grid\n    - top\u2011right: original rotated 90\u00b0 clockwise\n    - bottom\u2011left: original rotated 90\u00b0 counter\u2011clockwise\n    - bottom\u2011right: original rotated 180\u00b0\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(grid)\n    size = 2 * n\n    out = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            out[i][j] = grid[i][j]                         # original\n            out[i][j + n] = grid[n - 1 - j][i]             # rotate 90\u00b0 CW\n            out[i + n][j] = grid[j][n - 1 - i]             # rotate 90\u00b0 CCW\n            out[i + n][j + n] = grid[n - 1 - i][n - 1 - j] # rotate 180\u00b0\n    return out\n\n# Optional: allow running the script directly for manual testing.\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n\n    lines = [line.strip() for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]\n    if not lines:\n        sys.exit(0)\n\n    grid = [list(map(int, line.split())) for line in lines]\n    result = solve(grid)\n    for row in result:\n        print(' '.join(map(str, row)))",
  "script": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(grid: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform an N\u00d7N grid into a 2N\u00d72N grid composed of four quadrants:\n    - top\u2011left: original grid\n    - top\u2011right: original rotated 90\u00b0 clockwise\n    - bottom\u2011left: original rotated 90\u00b0 counter\u2011clockwise\n    - bottom\u2011right: original rotated 180\u00b0\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(grid)\n    size = 2 * n\n    out = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            out[i][j] = grid[i][j]                         # original\n            out[i][j + n] = grid[n - 1 - j][i]             # rotate 90\u00b0 CW\n            out[i + n][j] = grid[j][n - 1 - i]             # rotate 90\u00b0 CCW\n            out[i + n][j + n] = grid[n - 1 - i][n - 1 - j] # rotate 180\u00b0\n    return out\n\n# Optional: allow running the script directly for manual testing.\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n\n    lines = [line.strip() for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]\n    if not lines:\n        sys.exit(0)\n\n    grid = [list(map(int, line.split())) for line in lines]\n    result = solve(grid)\n    for row in result:\n        print(' '.join(map(str, row)))",
